fixture zone1_08_strike_on_the_way_down
doc BUILD.md s5 tech 8 "Attack-cancel landing: landing never interrupts an attack"; s6 Taper side 1 (2 f startup, 4 f active, 68 u reach); docs/adr/0010 Landing (0 f of lag); docs/adr/0013 Enemies (telegraph 24 f, swing 4 f active, recovery 20 f)
room zone1/08_attack_cancel_landing
spawn 74 480
frames 230
input
  0..58 R
  59 R attack
  60..121 R
  122 R attack
  123..177 R
  178 R attack
  179..229 R
end
expect
  # Drop 1, the safe dummy: the strike is pressed 4 f before the landing, so its active frames
  # (3 to 6) are the landing's last 2 airborne frames and its first 2 grounded ones. The landing
  # frame (63) is the strike's frame 5, live, and the dummy dies on it.
  at 58 state=air action=none
  at 59 action=side1 action_frame=1 state=air
  at 62 state=air action_frame=4 strike=1
  at 63 event.land=1 state=ground action=side1 action_frame=5 strike=1 event.kill=1 enemy.state=dead
  # Drop 2: the dummy's swing is already telegraphed and would land on frame 127 (its first
  # active tick). The strike kills it on the landing frame, a tick before: nothing lands on Ash.
  at 126 event.land=1 state=ground action=side1 action_frame=5 event.kill=1 enemy1.state=dead
  # Drop 3: the same again, the swing due on frame 183.
  at 182 event.land=1 state=ground action=side1 action_frame=5 event.kill=1 enemy2.state=dead
  never 0..229 hearts<5
  # The strike goes on through the landing to its last frame, 14, and the run never stops.
  at 194 action=side1 action_frame=14
  at 195 action=none
  mark through 1..229 event.room=1
  at through room=zone1_09_reverse_pogo state=ground
end
